@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] launch-guard-no-elevation-or-diagnostics
The guard MUST run without setuid bits or file capabilities, accept only fixed
absolute argv, keep stdout silent and record no logs. Operational events belong
to the caller's Lilly.Events catalog; intent bytes and paths never become
diagnostics from this process.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] launch-guard-custody-boundaries
Only private, single-link, zero-size intent lock files and exactly-53-byte
private intent payloads may authorize jailer exec: placement UUID, epoch and
generation must equal the requested values and the state byte must mark a
running generation. Exec MUST fail closed (71) and the shared intent lock MUST
survive exec so jailer's eventual descriptor close cannot leave an unfenced
process outside unit cleanup. Hegel properties cover the argument selector,
frame oracle and file refusal matrix; lock-across-exec is verified with real
processes in the sandbox.
